  <article class="ws-article">
    <p>An agent connected to <code>/mcp</code> with a project connection (OAuth or a project token) is offered 82 tools. A member token adds six account tools and a required <code>project</code> argument on every project tool, 88 in all. Each tool runs through the same REST routes the editor uses, as the connection's role, limited to its capabilities. Setup: <a href="{{sw-url '/docs/guides/ai-agents'}}">Connect an AI agent</a>.</p>
    <p>The list is generated from the server and committed to the repository (<code>contract/mcp-tools.json</code>, <code>contract/mcp-tools-member.json</code>), so a removed or renamed tool shows up as a diff in review. Sitewright is pre-1.0, so that is a record, not a compatibility promise.</p>

    <h2 id="capabilities">Capabilities</h2>
    <p>A connection carries a set of capabilities; the "Needs" column below names the one a tool checks. A dash means the tool is offered on every connection; calls that reach project content are still checked by the API behind it.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Allows</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>content:read</code></td><td>Reading pages, content, media, submissions, statistics, orders and bookings.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>content:write</code></td><td>Creating and changing content, media and settings; answering bookings; order fulfilment.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>content:delete</code></td><td>Deleting pages, entities, media and languages. Not implied by <code>content:write</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>publish</code></td><td>Deploying to Local Hosting.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>deploy</code></td><td>Managing and deploying FTP, FTPS, SFTP and git targets.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>payments:provider:write</code></td><td>Writing instance-wide payment provider definitions. Honored only on a connection owned by an instance admin.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Member tokens can also carry account capabilities: <code>projects:create</code>, <code>projects:rename</code>, <code>projects:delete</code>, <code>members:manage</code> and <code>members:invite</code>.</p>

    <h2 id="connect">Connection and discovery</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Needs</th><th class="min-w-56">Does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>get_scope</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>Whether the connection is authenticated, and its project, role and capabilities. Call it first.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>login</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>Starts a sign-in on the deprecated local bridge. On <code>/mcp</code> the token is fixed and this answers that it is not available.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>switch_project</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>Re-authenticates for another project on the deprecated local bridge. On <code>/mcp</code>, add another connection instead.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>get_capabilities</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>One index of everything the platform can do and where each part is documented.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>get_reference</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>Every <code>sw-*</code> helper, <code>data-sw-*</code> directive, binding namespace and loop variable.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>get_guide</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>The how-to for one feature area: design, components, images, effects, i18n, shop, payments, consent, templates, icons, nav, import, datasets.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>get_components</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>The markup contracts of the ten components.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>search_icons</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>Finds icon names: Phosphor glyphs, brand logos, country flags.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>search_textures</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>Finds tileable background textures, with ready CSS.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>search_google_fonts</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap">–</td><td>Searches the bundled Google Fonts catalog; makes no request to Google.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
