    <h2 id="member">Member token account tools</h2>
    <p>Only on a member token, which reaches every project its owner can open. Call <code>list_projects</code> first and pass the chosen id as <code>project</code> to every project tool; nothing is remembered between calls.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Needs</th><th class="min-w-56">Does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>list_projects</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>content:read</code></td><td>The projects the token reaches, with id, name, slug and role.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>create_project</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>projects:create</code></td><td>A new project with a home page and default navigation. Counts toward a daily limit.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>duplicate_project</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>projects:create</code></td><td>Copies a project (pages, content, settings, media) as "&lt;name&gt; (copy)". Also needs <code>content:read</code> on the source.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>list_members</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>members:manage</code></td><td>Members and pending invites of a project the token's owner owns.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>invite_member</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>members:invite</code></td><td>Invites a person by email; returns the invite and a one-time accept token.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>approve_invite</code></td><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>members:invite</code></td><td>Adds an invited person now. A new account gets a temporary password, shown once, valid for a week.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="tips">Working with the tools</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Edit, don't replace.</strong> <code>put_page</code> is a total replace: omitted fields are deleted. Use <code>patch_page</code>, <code>patch_text</code> and <code>patch_critical_css</code> for partial changes, and <code>put_content</code> with <code>merge:true</code> for settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Look at the result.</strong> <code>preview_page</code> returns screenshots of unsaved work, so an agent can check a layout before saving it.</li>
      <li><strong>Find before assuming.</strong> <code>get_capabilities</code> maps common needs to the tool or guide that covers them.</li>
      <li><strong>Untrusted text stays data.</strong> Buyer fields, booking notes, form submissions and search queries are typed by strangers; the tool descriptions tell agents never to follow them as instructions or publish them.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="ws-callout ws-callout-warn"><p class="!mt-0"><strong>Deprecated:</strong> <code>publish_project</code> (use <code>deploy_project</code>), and the local stdio bridge, the only place <code>login</code> and <code>switch_project</code> still work. Connect to <code>/mcp</code> over HTTP instead.</p></div>

